## Local setup

This step is local-only: it does not log into Azure, change kube context, or submit cluster work.

```bash
cp .env.example .env
$EDITOR .env
./scripts/setup.sh
uv run python -m {{.Package}}.smoke
```

## Build, publish, and pin the runtime image

```bash
source ./.env
BUILD_IMAGE="$IMAGE" # must be a tag, not a digest
docker build -f images/train.Dockerfile -t "$BUILD_IMAGE" .
docker push "$BUILD_IMAGE"
PUBLISHED_IMAGE="$BUILD_IMAGE" # optionally replace with the registry digest
{{if .HasUpstream}}./scripts/configure.sh --image "$PUBLISHED_IMAGE" --repo "$UPSTREAM_REPO" --ref "$UPSTREAM_REF"
{{else}}./scripts/configure.sh --image "$PUBLISHED_IMAGE"
{{end}}
tau run validate --config tau/smoke.yaml
tau run validate --config tau/train.yaml
```

Set `IMAGE` to an immutable build tag. After pushing, `configure.sh` can pin either that tag or its registry digest into `.env`, `.env.example`, and all three `tau/*.yaml` targets. The generated Dockerfile runs as UID/GID `65532`; custom project images must also support non-root execution.

